%% UML sequence — two officers co-edit an event announcement draft, then both try to publish
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor A as Officer A (Web App)
  actor B as Officer B (Web App)
  participant RT as Realtime Gateway (K-RT)
  participant CO as Collaboration (K-COLLAB)
  participant PO as Audience Policy (K-POLICY)
  participant R as Redis (C-REDIS)
  participant DB as PostgreSQL (C-DB)

  A->>RT: WSS connect /ws/drafts/42 (session token)
  RT->>PO: can_act(A, edit, draft 42)?
  PO-->>RT: allowed (officer of community 7)
  RT->>CO: join(room draft:42, A)
  CO->>DB: load snapshot + updates after snapshot
  DB-->>CO: Yjs state (version 16)
  CO-->>A: sync-step-2 {state, version: 16}, presence [A]
  B->>RT: WSS connect /ws/drafts/42
  Note over RT,CO: same authorization and sync as A
  CO-->>B: sync-step-2 {state, version: 16}, presence [A, B]

  par concurrent edits to the same sentence
    A->>RT: yjs-update {bytes, client_id: A}
    RT->>CO: apply(update A)
    CO->>DB: INSERT draft_update (append-only)
    CO->>R: PUBLISH draft:42 update A
    R-->>RT: update A (fan-out to every API instance)
    RT-->>B: yjs-update A
  and
    B->>RT: yjs-update {bytes, client_id: B}
    RT->>CO: apply(update B)
    CO->>DB: INSERT draft_update
    CO->>R: PUBLISH draft:42 update B
    R-->>RT: update B
    RT-->>A: yjs-update B
  end
  Note over A,B: CRDT merge is order-independent, so A and B<br/>converge to the same text and neither edit is lost

  alt saving an update fails (DB unavailable)
    CO-->>A: error {code: SAVE_FAILED, retry: true}
    Note over A: Client keeps the update locally and resends<br/>after backoff, banner "Not saved yet"
  end

  par both officers press Publish
    A->>CO: POST /api/v1/drafts/42/publish {expected_version: 17}
  and
    B->>CO: POST /api/v1/drafts/42/publish {expected_version: 17}
  end
  CO->>DB: BEGIN, UPDATE drafts SET status='published', version=18<br/>WHERE id=42 AND version=17 AND status='editing'
  DB-->>CO: 1 row updated (A's request wins the row lock)
  CO->>DB: INSERT post (sanitized HTML from Yjs state), INSERT event, COMMIT
  CO-->>A: 201 Created {post_id: 913}
  CO->>DB: same conditional UPDATE for B's request
  DB-->>CO: 0 rows updated
  CO-->>B: 409 Conflict {code: ALREADY_PUBLISHED, post_id: 913}
  CO->>R: PUBLISH community:7 post.created {post_id: 913}
  R-->>RT: post.created
  RT-->>A: event post.created (draft room closed, read-only)
  RT-->>B: event post.created (draft room closed, read-only)

  opt B's connection drops during editing
    Note over B,RT: B's client buffers local updates, on reconnect it sends<br/>its state vector and receives only the missing updates
  end
